   178	/// `MultifaceSpreader.SpreadConfig#placeBlock` split across the sync/async boundary.
   179	///
   180	/// Placing a block needs to both read (`canSpreadInto`, already covered by
   181	/// `SpreadConfig`) and write the target block. Writes in this codebase go through
   182	/// `World::set_block_state`, which is async, so the actual placement step is a separate
   183	/// trait a consumer implements around its own world reference — this mirrors
   184	/// `DefaultSpreaderConfig` wrapping a `MultifaceBlock` reference in vanilla.
   185	///
   186	/// `accessor()` must reflect the same live world `place()` writes to, so that
   187	/// `spread_all`/`spread_from_face_toward_all_directions` see each write before
