   117	/// `MultifaceBlock.canAttachTo`.
   118	///
   119	/// Vanilla checks `isFaceFull` against both the neighbour's block-support shape and
   120	/// its collision shape. This codebase has no per-direction shape query yet, only the
   121	/// coarser "is this side sturdy" flag (`BlockState::is_side_solid`, itself documented
   122	/// as `isFaceSturdy()` in Java) already used for the same purpose by
   123	/// `abstract_wall_mounting.rs`'s `WallMountedBlock::can_place_at`. Using it here is a
   124	/// known simplification, not full shape-based parity, until per-direction voxel shapes
   125	/// exist in `pumpkin_data`.
