    22	//! `.lightLevel(...)`, no `.randomTicks()`, and no `randomTick` override in
    23	//! `SculkVeinBlock.java` — sculk vein growth is driven entirely by
    24	//! `SculkSpreader::update_cursors` (Step 4), never by a block random tick. Neither does
    25	//! `GlowLichenBlock.java` override `randomTick` (also confirmed by reading it in full),
    26	//! so this is not sculk-vein-specific; unlike sculk vein, glow lichen *does* emit light
    27	//! (`.lightLevel(GlowLichenBlock.emission(7))` in `Blocks.java`, confirmed by
    28	//! `pumpkin-data`'s generated `Block::GLOW_LICHEN` states showing `luminance: 7` once
    29	//! any face is present) — `Block::SCULK_VEIN`'s states are all `luminance: 0`.
