The audit confirms all four are already represented, at least partially, under architectural names that the matcher misses:

- `DistanceManager`: `ChunkLoading`, active-chunk tracking, chunk scheduling, and player chunker paths.
- `BambooStalkBlock`: `BambooBlock` plus `BambooSaplingBlock`.
- `LiquidBlock`: the `FluidBehaviour`/flowing-fluid system, fluid physics, registry dispatch, and bucket paths.
- `MultifaceBlock`: `abstract_multiface`, `multiface_spreader`, `MultifaceGrowthBlock`, and `SculkVeinBlock`.

Because the worklist explicitly says partial coverage is a successful `NOT_A_GAP`, I’m making no implementation changes. I’m recording the exact decompile ranges and existing call sites now.
All four candidates have existing Rust behavior under renamed/shared architectural implementations; no new feature code is authorized by the worklist rules.
